# vrc-dcc-workstation — Cursor rules

Authoritative file: root `AGENTS.md`.

Skeleton VRChat DCC station (Blender + Unity 2022.3). No third-party binaries in git.

Same shape as debugger-workstation: skill descriptions **guide** auto-apply. Do not require a passphrase.

## Job (intent)

If the task is clearly VRChat **avatar** / clothes / menus / avatar Blender-Unity DCC work **in this clone**, follow `templates/JOB.md`, `skills/vrc-dcc/references/dcc-session.md`, and `skills/vrc-dcc/references/slice-loop.md`. `python maps/handshake.py <avatar>` then `python maps/gate.py <avatar> begin <id>` then named `vrc_*` (not invented `execute_code`). Do **not** run the install questionnaire. Do not wait to be named. No default avatar. Worlds / Udon: `skills/vrc-world`. Clothes vs USB vs C#: `maps/GRAPHS.md`. Probe prints `graphs:` / `codegraph_*`.

If the ask is clearly **not** VRChat (generic app/web/library, other game engines, Blender film): do **not** handshake, do not attach Blender/Unity MCP, do not apply 改模 playbooks. Skills stay in this clone — never user-global.

## Install / bootstrap only

When the owner asks to initialize / install / set up **this clone**: resolve locale (`docs/I18N.md`) → explore (`AGENTS.md`, gitignored `OWNER.md`) → ask (`templates/INIT_QUESTIONNAIRE.md`) → plan → `bootstrap.ps1`. Chat in the resolved locale. Git commits stay English. Stop lines cannot be waived in chat; see `docs/MAINTAIN.md`.

MCP: project / `--mcp-config` only. Never user-global. One blender-mcp client at a time.

Human clicks VRChat SDK Build & Publish. Official Unity 6 MCP stays off 2022.3 avatar projects. Do not write the avatar Unity project from a home cwd.
